# quantum-site — a static site generator for the Quantum language
#
# Turns a folder of Markdown pages, Handlebars-style layouts and static files into a
# complete website: blog with tags and archive, RSS feed, sitemap, relative links that
# work on GitHub Pages or straight from disk.
#
#   Global        Module              What it does
#   ────────────  ──────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#   SiteUtil      src/util.sa         slugify, escaping, dates, paths, file helpers
#   FrontMatter   src/frontmatter.sa  "---" metadata blocks (YAML subset)
#   Markdown      src/markdown.sa     Markdown -> HTML, headings, table of contents
#   Template      src/template.sa     {{ }} templates: if/each/with, partials, filters
#   Site          src/site.sa         builds content/ + layouts/ + static/ -> public/
#   SiteStarter   src/starter.sa      the starter site written by `init`
#
# Bundle entry: lists the modules in dependency order. Use it with `# @use quantum-site`
# and quantum-bundle, or run the pre-bundled single files in dist/.

# @use ./src/util.sa
# @use ./src/frontmatter.sa
# @use ./src/markdown.sa
# @use ./src/template.sa
# @use ./src/site.sa
# @use ./src/starter.sa
